author ai
group gui/graph
note Drawing one frame of the graph canvas. The whole canvas is a single element with a custom draw function, so there is no element per node and no hit testing from the element tree: the scene is built in window pixels, the rectangles it produced are kept, and next frame's clicks are resolved against them. Pan and zoom are the app's own two fields rather than a transform - the node font size is the UI size times the zoom, rounded to a whole pixel, so text is rasterised at the size it is drawn and never scaled. Edges are painted before nodes so nodes sit on top: grey curves for calls, thick green ones for the steps of a path, and a short orange one for a callee that sits left of its caller instead of a wire across the canvas.

